# Platform Control Center — domains, health, audit (P1 EPIC F)

## Create tenant dev hint

`POST /platform/v1/tenants` success body may include optional **`devHostHint`** when `PLATFORM_ROOT_DOMAIN` is `localhost` (dev only). Prod `sites` URLs unchanged.

```json
{
  "devHostHint": {
    "marketingHost": "my-club.localhost",
    "portalHost": "my-club.portal.localhost",
    "adminHost": "my-club.admin.localhost"
  }
}
```

## Custom domains

Prisma model **`TenantDomain`** (`tenant_domains`):

| Column | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `hostname` | Custom hostname (unique) |
| `tenantId` | Owning tenant |
| `surface` | `marketing` \| `portal` |
| `status` | `pending` \| `verified` |
| `cnameTarget` | Expected CNAME target (platform subdomain host) |

Repository: `PlatformDomainRepository` — admin Prisma only (no tenant RLS).

### Domain API

| Method | Path | Body |
|--------|------|------|
| `GET` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/domains` | — |
| `POST` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/domains` | `{ hostname, surface? }` |
| `DELETE` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/domains/{domainId}` | — |
| `POST` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/domains/{domainId}/verify` | — |

POST returns `{ domain, cnameInstructions: { hostname, cnameTarget } }`. Verify performs **live DNS CNAME lookup** when `PLATFORM_DOMAIN_DNS_LOOKUP` is enabled (default on); dev bypass via `PLATFORM_DOMAIN_VERIFY_STUB=pass`. On verify success, **SSL provision** runs via `PLATFORM_SSL_PROVIDER` (`stub` default · `cloudflare` optional).

### SSL columns (P2-D)

| Column | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `sslStatus` | `pending` \| `active` \| `failed` |
| `sslExpiresAt` | cert expiry |
| `sslLastError` | last provision error |
| `lastObservedCname` | live DNS observation |

### SSL ops API (P2-D)

| Method | Path | Notes |
|--------|------|-------|
| GET | `/platform/v1/domains/ssl-summary` | `{ expiringWithin14Days }` |
| POST | `/platform/v1/domains/run-ssl-expiry-check` | owner · audit `DOMAIN_SSL_EXPIRING` |

Detail: [`platform-domains-ssl.mdoc`](platform-domains-ssl.mdoc).

## Site health

| Method | Path | Response |
|--------|------|----------|
| `GET` | `/platform/v1/tenants/{tenantId}/sites/check` | `{ results: { marketing, portal, admin } }` each `{ url, ok, status }` |

Issues concurrent `HEAD` requests to the three provisioned URLs (`buildClubSiteUrls`).

### Overview unhealthy KPI

The platform **Overview** card `unhealthyCount` is computed server-side in `loadPlatformOverviewStats`:

1. `GET /platform/v1/tenants?limit=100&offset=0` loads the current tenant page.
2. For each tenant with `status === "active"` (up to **`PLATFORM_OVERVIEW_HEALTH_CHECK_LIMIT`**, default **25**), the BFF calls `GET /platform/v1/tenants/{id}/sites/check`.
3. Each check response contributes `countUnhealthySiteChecks(results)` — one increment per surface where `ok === false` (marketing, portal, admin).
4. Failed or skipped health checks contribute **0** (overview stays usable when a club is unreachable).

This caps overview latency when many clubs exist; raise the env limit only in environments where full-fleet health is required on every overview load.

Pure aggregation lives in `platform-overview-aggregation.ts` (`aggregateUnhealthySiteCount`); `loadPlatformOverviewStats` wires it to `proxyPlatformApi`. Behavioral tests: `load-platform-overview-stats.spec.ts` (not only `count-unhealthy-from-sites-check` helper).

## Platform audit log

| Method | Path |
|--------|------|
| `GET` | `/platform/v1/audit?limit=50&offset=0` |

Response: `{ items: PlatformAuditEventDto[], total, limit, offset }` — platform events only (`platform_audit_events`), not tenant `audit_events`.

## Web

| Surface | Path |
|---------|------|
| Club detail **Domains** tab | list + add + CNAME + verify |
| Club detail **Sites** tab | Check health button |
| Audit page | `/platform/audit` |
| Overview | `unhealthyCount` KPI card |
| Nav | Audit link |

BFF mirrors `/api/platform/tenants/{id}/domains`, `.../sites/check`, `/api/platform/audit`.

## Verify (EPIC F gate)

```bash
pnpm --filter @apps/api exec node --test \
  test/platform-tenants-domains.spec.ts \
  test/platform-audit-list.spec.ts \
  test/platform-sites-check.spec.ts \
  test/create-tenant-response-dto.spec.ts

cd apps/web && NODE_ENV=test node --import tsx --import ./test/register-dom.mjs --test --test-force-exit \
  test/platform-bff-domains.spec.ts \
  test/tab-domains.spec.ts \
  test/platform-audit-page.spec.ts \
  test/platform-nav.spec.ts
```
